  "goodToKnow": "Die Chronik is a chronicle: a record of events in chronological order, historically a town or monastery's annals. Today it's also used in news, such as Chronik on a newspaper page for local incidents. The adjective chronisch means chronic (eine chronische Krankheit), the adverb chronologisch means in time order, and der Chronist is the chronicler. The Greek root chronos (time) is the same."
